"""Young adults: an opening hook, a line to carry away, a check for understanding and the common misreadings for each lesson."""
R = {
'YA-1-1': dict(hook='Ask the group to write, privately, the question about God they would most like answered. Collect them anonymously and read two aloud.', mem='“You have made us for yourself, O Lord, and our heart is restless until it rests in you.” (Augustine)', assess='Ask each person to state, in two sentences, one reason reason can point to God and one limit of that reasoning.', misc=['“Faith and reason are opposites.”', '“Arguments for God are meant to force belief.”']),
'YA-1-2': dict(hook='Ask the group to draw the Trinity in 30 seconds, then compare drawings. Which pictures help? Which mislead?', mem='“Go and make disciples… baptizing them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit.” (Matthew 28:19)', assess='Ask each person to explain why the Trinity is not three gods and not one God in three masks.', misc=['“The Trinity is a math puzzle.”', '“The Father is God, the Son is half-God.”']),
'YA-1-3': dict(hook='Ask: “If a friend asked who Jesus is, what would you say in one sentence?” Collect answers, then read Mark 8:27–30.', mem='“You are the Christ, the Son of the living God.” (Matthew 16:16)', assess='Ask each person to list two claims Jesus makes about himself and what follows if they are true.', misc=['“Jesus never claimed to be God.”', '“Jesus is just a great moral teacher.”']),
'YA-2-1': dict(hook='Show a hand-copied page and a printed page. Ask how we can trust that an ancient text has been passed on well.', mem='“All Scripture is inspired by God and profitable.” (2 Timothy 3:16)', assess='Ask each person to explain inspiration, the canon and one way to read a hard passage well.', misc=['“The Bible fell from heaven.”', '“The Church invented the Bible to control people.”']),
'YA-2-2': dict(hook='Ask: “How do you know what your grandparents were like if you never met them?” Link to oral and written handing-on.', mem='“Stand firm and hold to the traditions that you were taught.” (2 Thessalonians 2:15)', assess='Ask each person to describe how Scripture, Tradition and the Magisterium work together.', misc=['“Tradition means whatever is old.”', '“The Magisterium adds new revelation.”']),
'YA-2-3': dict(hook='Poll: “Have you ever said ‘I like Jesus but not the Church’? What makes you say it?” Listen without defending.', mem='“Where two or three are gathered in my name, there am I in the midst of them.” (Matthew 18:20)', assess='Ask each person to give two reasons the Church is more than an institution and one honest struggle.', misc=['“Spiritual but not religious is enough.”', '“The Church is only its scandals.”']),
'YA-3-1': dict(hook='Set a ten-second silence. Ask: “What was your mind doing?” Name the experience of distraction.', mem='“Lord, teach us to pray.” (Luke 11:1)', assess='Ask each person to name one obstacle in their prayer and one remedy they will try.', misc=['“If prayer feels dry, God is absent.”', '“Prayer is only asking for things.”']),
'YA-3-2': dict(hook='Read Psalm 23 first fast, then slowly with pauses. Ask what changed.', mem='“Your word is a lamp to my feet and a light to my path.” (Psalm 119:105)', assess='Ask each person to describe the four movements of lectio divina and share one word that stood out.', misc=['“Lectio divina is an Eastern technique.”', '“It replaces study of Scripture.”']),
'YA-3-3': dict(hook='Ask: “What do you bring to Mass besides yourself?” Invite one thing to offer this Sunday.', mem='“Do this in remembrance of me.” (Luke 22:19)', assess='Ask each person to name the parts of the Mass and one way to participate more fully.', misc=['“Mass is a performance I watch.”', '“I get nothing out of it, so it’s pointless.”']),
'YA-4-1': dict(hook='Ask: “What do people mean when they say ‘that’s not a big deal’? When is that true and false?”', mem='“If we say we have no sin, we deceive ourselves.” (1 John 1:8)', assess='Ask each person to define mortal and venial sin and explain the three conditions for mortal sin.', misc=['“Sin is just breaking arbitrary rules.”', '“I am too bad to be forgiven.”']),
'YA-4-2': dict(hook='Read the Prodigal Son. Ask: “Who runs? Who waits? What does the father say?”', mem='“Whose sins you forgive are forgiven them.” (John 20:23)', assess='Ask each person to list the four parts of Confession and answer “Why a priest?”', misc=['“Confession is a magic eraser.”', '“The priest can tell others.”']),
'YA-4-3': dict(hook='Ask silently: “Who is hardest to forgive?” Hold the question; do not share.', mem='“Forgive us our trespasses as we forgive those who trespass against us.” (Our Father)', assess='Ask each person to explain what forgiveness is not and one step toward it.', misc=['“Forgiving means forgetting.”', '“Forgiving means staying in danger.”']),
'YA-5-1': dict(hook='Hold up water, oil, bread and a ring. Ask what each is used for and what happens when God uses them.', mem='“Unless one is born of water and the Spirit, he cannot enter the kingdom of God.” (John 3:5)', assess='Ask each person to name the seven sacraments with their matter and form.', misc=['“Sacraments are symbols only.”', '“Sacraments work apart from faith.”']),
'YA-5-2': dict(hook='Read John 6:60–69. Ask: “Why did many leave? Why did Peter stay?”', mem='“Lord, to whom shall we go? You have the words of eternal life.” (John 6:68)', assess='Ask each person to explain transubstantiation in plain words and cite two texts.', misc=['“The Eucharist is a symbol.”', '“Catholics believe in cannibalism.”']),
'YA-5-3': dict(hook='Ask: “What would change if you took your baptism as seriously as a wedding?”', mem='“Do you not know that all of us who have been baptized into Christ Jesus were baptized into his death?” (Romans 6:3)', assess='Ask each person to name what Baptism and Confirmation do and one concrete way to live them.', misc=['“Baptism is a family tradition.”', '“Confirmation is graduation.”']),
'YA-6-1': dict(hook='Ask: “What do films and songs say love is? What do they leave out?” Take a few answers.', mem='“So God created man in his own image… male and female he created them.” (Genesis 1:27)', assess='Ask each person to state what the Church means by love and what gift of self requires.', misc=['“The Church thinks the body is bad.”', '“Love is just a feeling.”']),
'YA-6-2': dict(hook='Ask: “What makes a relationship healthy? What are red flags?” List both columns.', mem='“Above all else, guard your heart, for everything you do flows from it.” (Proverbs 4:23)', assess='Ask each person to draft three boundaries and one question for discernment.', misc=['“Dating is only for marriage-ready people.”', '“Boundaries mean you do not trust.”']),
'YA-6-3': dict(hook='Say plainly that this is a topic where shame can silence people, and that the focus is on freedom and healing, not blame.', mem='“So if the Son sets you free, you will be free indeed.” (John 8:36)', assess='Ask each person to name two practical steps toward freedom (accountability, filters, confession, counsel).', misc=['“Everyone does it, so it does no harm.”', '“I can fix this entirely on my own.”']),
'YA-7-1': dict(hook='Ask: “Where have you felt most alive? Where do you feel you are most useful?”', mem='“Speak, Lord, for your servant hears.” (1 Samuel 3:9)', assess='Ask each person to describe the universal call to holiness and one step in discernment.', misc=['“Only some are called.”', '“If I choose wrong, I ruin my life.”']),
'YA-7-2': dict(hook='Ask: “What do you most want your future family to be like?” Write three words.', mem='“What therefore God has joined together, let not man put asunder.” (Mark 10:9)', assess='Ask each person to name the four goods of marriage and what preparing for it requires now.', misc=['“Marriage is a contract renewable at will.”', '“A Catholic marriage guarantees happiness.”']),
'YA-7-3': dict(hook='Ask: “What would you give your life to? What would you need to let go?”', mem='“Follow me, and I will make you fishers of men.” (Matthew 4:19)', assess='Ask each person to describe celibacy as a gift and how single people can live a vocation.', misc=['“Priests and nuns are less happy.”', '“Single life is a failure.”']),
'YA-8-1': dict(hook='Ask: “Is your work a job, a career or a calling? What changes if it is a calling?”', mem='“Whatever you do, work heartily, as for the Lord.” (Colossians 3:23)', assess='Ask each person to write how their work or study can serve others and glorify God.', misc=['“Only religious jobs are holy.”', '“Work is a curse.”']),
'YA-8-2': dict(hook='Ask for a quick estimate: how much of your income would you give away if you could? Reflect on why.', mem='“You cannot serve God and mammon.” (Matthew 6:24)', assess='Ask each person to describe the universal destination of goods and one practice of generosity.', misc=['“Money is evil.”', '“What I earn is entirely mine.”']),
'YA-8-3': dict(hook='Show a map of a local need. Ask: “Who is missing from our conversations?”', mem='“He has told you, O man, what is good; and what does the Lord require of you but to do justice, and to love kindness, and to walk humbly with your God?” (Micah 6:8)', assess='Ask each person to name four principles of Catholic social teaching and apply one.', misc=['“Social teaching belongs to one party.”', '“Charity is enough; justice is optional.”']),
'YA-9-1': dict(hook='Acknowledge that real suffering lives in the room. Invite quiet before beginning. Offer to step out.', mem='“I consider that the sufferings of this present time are not worth comparing with the glory that is to be revealed to us.” (Romans 8:18)', assess='Ask each person to state what the Church does and does not say about why God allows suffering.', misc=['“Suffering is always punishment.”', '“A good God would prevent all evil.”']),
'YA-9-2': dict(hook='Ask: “Where did you first hear that faith and science disagree? Who said it?”', mem='“The heavens declare the glory of God.” (Psalm 19:1)', assess='Ask each person to explain how Genesis 1 and science answer different questions.', misc=['“Catholics must reject evolution.”', '“Science has disproved God.”']),
'YA-9-3': dict(hook='Ask about a friend of another faith or none. What do you admire? What do you not understand?', mem='“That they may all be one.” (John 17:21)', assess='Ask each person to explain how the Church can say Christ is the only Savior and still respect other religions.', misc=['“All religions teach the same.”', '“Respect means silence about your beliefs.”']),
'YA-10-1': dict(hook='Ask: “Who is one person who would tell you the truth if you were off track?”', mem='“Let us consider how to stir up one another to love and good works.” (Hebrews 10:24)', assess='Ask each person to name a community, an accountability partner and one commitment.', misc=['“I can be a Christian alone.”', '“Accountability means being judged.”']),
'YA-10-2': dict(hook='Ask: “When did someone share their faith with you in a way you appreciated?”', mem='“Always be prepared to make a defense to anyone who calls you to account for the hope that is in you.” (1 Peter 3:15)', assess='Ask each person to write a 60-second story of faith and one invitation to offer.', misc=['“Sharing faith is pushy.”', '“I need to be an expert first.”']),
'YA-10-3': dict(hook='Ask: “What is one practice that would change your week if you kept it?”', mem='“Pray without ceasing.” (1 Thessalonians 5:17)', assess='Ask each person to present a rule with daily, weekly and monthly practices.', misc=['“A rule of life is legalism.”', '“If I miss a day, I have failed.”']),
'YA-11-1': dict(hook='Ask: “What does it mean for a teaching to ‘develop’ without changing?” Take answers.', mem='“When the Spirit of truth comes, he will guide you into all the truth.” (John 16:13)', assess='Ask each person to explain infallibility and development of doctrine with one example.', misc=['“The Pope is infallible in everything.”', '“Doctrine never develops.”']),
'YA-11-2': dict(hook='Acknowledge that history includes real harm done by Catholics. Commit to honesty and humility.', mem='“There is neither Jew nor Greek, there is neither slave nor free, there is neither male nor female, for you are all one in Christ Jesus.” (Galatians 3:28)', assess='Ask each person to name one historical wrong, what the Church has said and what repair requires.', misc=['“The Church never did wrong.”', '“The Church is only a history of wrongs.”']),
'YA-11-3': dict(hook='Ask: “If you could ask Jesus’ mother for anything, what would it be?”', mem='“Blessed are you among women.” (Luke 1:42)', assess='Ask each person to describe four Marian dogmas and what honor differs from worship.', misc=['“Catholics worship Mary.”', '“Marian devotion competes with Christ.”']),
'YA-12-1': dict(hook='Ask: “When have you disagreed with someone you respect? How did you handle it?”', mem='“We must obey God rather than men.” (Acts 5:29)', assess='Ask each person to explain how to form a conscience and what it means to follow it.', misc=['“Conscience means doing what I want.”', '“Obedience means silence.”']),
'YA-12-2': dict(hook='Ask: “What is one issue where your faith shapes how you vote or act?”', mem='“Render to Caesar the things that are Caesar’s, and to God the things that are God’s.” (Matthew 22:21)', assess='Ask each person to apply three principles of Catholic social teaching to a civic issue.', misc=['“Faith has no place in politics.”', '“One party is the Catholic party.”']),
'YA-12-3': dict(hook='Read Psalm 88 aloud. Ask: “What do you notice? How does it end?” (In darkness.)', mem='“O Lord, God of my salvation, I cry out day and night before you.” (Psalm 88:1)', assess='Ask each person to name signs of dryness, doubt and depression, and who they could talk to.', misc=['“Doubt is a sin.”', '“If I feel nothing, God is gone.”']),
}
